WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.855
Enable downstream and upstream logs in Settings.

2
00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:10.050
Turn on body recording when you need to inspect message contents, and
keep the default redaction enabled.

3
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:16.118
When a request fails, find its record by time, model, or request ID.

4
00:00:16.138 --> 00:00:18.992
Here, no upstream response arrived.

5
00:00:19.013 --> 00:00:23.800
The request URL in the details helps locate the configuration problem.

6
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.500
Check the provider address, restore the correct configuration, and send
the request again.

7
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.105
The new request returns HTTP 200.

8
00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:40.438
Compare the records before and after the change to confirm that the
connection is working again.

9
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:48.092
Filter global usage by user to inspect request counts, input and output
tokens, costs, and trends.

10
00:00:48.112 --> 00:00:51.912
You can also group the results by model or provider.

11
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.680
Open a usage record to inspect tokens and cost for an individual call.

12
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:03.475
Costs depend on your configured model prices and do not represent the
upstream account balance.
